            'detailed_explanation' => [
                'Compatible physical measurements describe the same quantity in different units. For factor-based conversions, the source value is multiplied by an exact or defined factor. One inch is exactly 2.54 centimetres, one international pound is exactly 0.45359237 kilograms, and one international mile is exactly 1.609344 kilometres.',
                'Temperature is different because Celsius, Fahrenheit and kelvin do not share the same zero point. Celsius to Fahrenheit multiplies by 9/5 and adds 32. Celsius to kelvin adds 273.15. A temperature below 0 K is below absolute zero, so the calculator rejects a conversion that would produce a negative kelvin value.',
